{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9c1c9a3e-6b2f-4b6a-8b1d-0f1a2b3c4d5e",
    "name": "Unified Service Scheduler",
    "description": "Manual/exploratory API testing for the Unified Service Scheduler assessment - mirrors the scenarios covered by Scheduler.IntegrationTests (see README.md's \"Integration Tests\" section). Booking times are computed by the collection-level pre-request script (Postman > this collection > Pre-request Script tab) instead of hardcoded, so every run targets a fresh, still-valid slot instead of a date that eventually lands in the past or collides with a slot already booked in a previous run.\n\nBefore running: start the API - `dotnet run --project src/Scheduler.Api` - and confirm `baseUrl` (a collection variable, Variables tab) matches, default `http://localhost:5207` (the default \"http\" launch profile).\n\nFolders:\n1. Happy Path & Validation - run top to bottom, or use Collection Runner.\n2. Double Booking (Sequential) - proves the guarantee holds when one request finishes before the next starts (the easy case).\n\nFor the project's actual concurrency requirement - many requests racing for the same slot with none of them finished before the others start - use `scripts/concurrency-demo.js` (`node scripts/concurrency-demo.js`) instead of Postman. Postman's Collection Runner sends requests sequentially, so it can't reproduce genuine concurrent dispatch; the Node script fires real parallel requests via Promise.all. See README.md's \"Concurrency demo script\" section.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const pad = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, \"0\");",
          "const now = new Date();",
          "",
          "// Clamp \"now\"'s time-of-day into the dealership's 08:00-16:00 operating window",
          "// (16:00 leaves an hour of room before the 17:00 close, enough for every seeded",
          "// service type including the 90-minute INTERIOR_CLEANING) so every run of this",
          "// collection - at whatever minute you happen to run it - targets a slot nobody",
          "// has booked yet, instead of colliding with whatever the last run already booked.",
          "// This is dealership-local wall-clock time deliberately, not UTC - operating hours",
          "// are a local-time concept (see AppointmentSchedulingPolicy in the Domain layer).",
          "const hour = Math.min(Math.max(now.getHours(), 8), 16);",
          "const minute = now.getMinutes();",
          "",
          "function businessDayIn(offsetDays) {",
          "  const d = new Date(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), now.getDate() + offsetDays);",
          "  if (d.getDay() === 0) {",
          "    d.setDate(d.getDate() + 1); // dealership is closed Sunday - roll to Monday",
          "  }",
          "  d.setHours(hour, minute, 0, 0);",
          "  return `${d.getFullYear()}-${pad(d.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(d.getDate())}T${pad(d.getHours())}:${pad(d.getMinutes())}:00`;",
          "}",
          "",
          "// Recomputed before every request in the collection, but deterministic within the",
          "// same clock minute - so as long as a full run finishes in well under a minute",
          "// (it will; each request is a few milliseconds), every request agrees on the same",
          "// set of times.",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"bookingStartTime\", businessDayIn(1));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"altBookingStartTime\", businessDayIn(2));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"doubleBookingStartTime\", businessDayIn(3));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"outsideHoursStartTime\", businessDayIn(1).slice(0, 11) + \"07:00:00\");"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
